WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:09.954
Hi! Who came first in the race? Where are you in the queue? Today we'll learn ordinal numbers, first to tenth.

2
00:00:10.104 --> 00:00:12.714
Three tells how many there are.

3
00:00:12.864 --> 00:00:15.306
Third tells the position.

4
00:00:15.456 --> 00:00:19.506
In English we write 1st, 2nd, 3rd, 4th.

5
00:00:19.656 --> 00:00:26.946
We say first, second, third, then add th: fourth, fifth.

6
00:00:27.096 --> 00:00:30.834
First check whether to count from the left or the right.

7
00:00:30.984 --> 00:00:35.658
Start from the left: one, two. That's the 2nd.

8
00:00:35.808 --> 00:00:38.970
The same thing might be 4th from the right.

9
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:42.930
In a queue, count from the front.

10
00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:47.946
Watch out! If it says from the left, don't count from the right!

11
00:00:48.096 --> 00:00:51.570
Find the side the question says and start there.

12
00:00:51.720 --> 00:00:56.082
Stop when you reach the position asked.

13
00:00:56.232 --> 00:01:04.914
Your turn! The fastest runner comes in which place? Pause and think.

14
00:01:05.064 --> 00:01:10.698
The fastest runner comes 1st. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:10.848 --> 00:01:21.426
Another one! Apple, banana, grapes, orange. What is 3rd from the left? Pause and think.

16
00:01:21.576 --> 00:01:27.570
One apple, two banana, three grapes. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:35.706
Here's another! What is 1st from the right? Pause and think.

18
00:01:35.856 --> 00:01:41.466
The first from the right is the orange. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:41.616 --> 00:01:49.410
Try one more! How do we say 2nd? Pause and think.

20
00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:54.426
2nd is second. Did you get it right?

21
00:01:54.576 --> 00:02:04.890
Try one more! 5 people queue and Mei is 2nd. How many are in front of her? Pause and think.

22
00:02:05.040 --> 00:02:11.538
She's 2nd, so only 1 person is in front. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:11.688 --> 00:02:19.866
Try one more! Do three and third mean the same? Pause and think.

24
00:02:20.016 --> 00:02:27.114
No. Three is how many; third is a position. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:27.264 --> 00:02:35.370
Try one more! Which position is tenth? Pause and think.

26
00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:40.146
Tenth is 10th. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:40.296 --> 00:02:48.330
Last one! Which position is first? Pause and think.

28
00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:53.321
First is 1st. Did you get it right?

29
00:02:53.471 --> 00:03:01.505
Remember: how many is an amount, and first, second, third are positions. Check which side to count from.

30
00:03:01.655 --> 00:03:07.961
Line up your family's shoes and say whose pair is first, second and third!

